  "note": "Election of the Donaghadee Urban Council, May 1958. There was no contest: seven nominations were received for nine seats, and a retiring member was deemed re-elected (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1958, p. 6). The first six were retiring members. Mr. C. C. Stewart, who served on the last council, lodged no nomination paper but was deemed re-elected unless he notified the town clerk within seven days; one seat remained to be filled. Returned unopposed."
